FSPEED-CTR-TRACE lane=gbdt-rank-yetirank MOJOLEARN_CTR_TRACE=1 (the fit prints its CTR config split and prep marker; DEVIATION 2634 is observable)
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-rank-yetirank arms=* metric=mismatch delta=1.000000 reason=grower: ours and CatBoost fit YetiRank on symmetric trees (ours has no other policy for a ranking loss); XGBoost depthwise at depth 6, LightGBM leaf-wise capped at depth 6 and 64 leaves, because neither has an oblivious grower
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-rank-yetirank arms=* metric=mismatch delta=2.000000 reason=objective: XGBoost rank:ndcg and LightGBM lambdarank are LambdaMART (NDCG-weighted pairwise gradients), a different loss from YetiRank's sampled permutations; each is that library's closest listwise objective, labeled
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-rank-yetirank arms=* metric=mismatch delta=3.000000 reason=l2 1.0 is pinned on every arm; the YetiRank default in CatBoost (and ours) is 0
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-rank-yetirank arms=* metric=mismatch delta=4.000000 reason=YetiRank draws its permutations from each library's own seeded generator (seed 7); the streams are not shared, so the fits differ by construction
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-rank-yetirank arms=* metric=mismatch delta=5.000000 reason=XGBoost pair construction (lambdarank_pair_method, lambdarank_num_pair_per_sample) and LightGBM's lambdarank_truncation_level (30) and label_gain (2^g - 1) are left at their defaults; no library exposes the others' pair sampling
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-rank-yetirank arms=* metric=mismatch delta=6.000000 reason=XGBoost is handed each query renumbered by order of appearance (it refuses unsorted qids); the same partition of the same rows in the same order
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-rank-yetirank arms=* metric=mismatch delta=7.000000 reason=LightGBM min_child_samples 20 and min_child_weight 1e-3 stay at its defaults: at 0 (the gbdt lanes' value) LightGBM 4.7.0 aborts the first lambdarank tree
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-rank-yetirank arms=* metric=objectives delta=4.000000 reason=catboost YetiRank; lightgbm lambdarank; mojolearn YetiRank; xgboost rank:ndcg
FSPEED-NOTE lane=gbdt-rank-yetirank arms=ours metric=devices delta=1.000000 reason=devices=gpu (explicit); on an NVIDIA box the vendors' CPU arms do not run, so a lane whose only opponent is a CPU library has NO legal opponent here and says so
